  "reason": "The best configuration found is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc 0.7250). The consistent evidence shows weighted fusion outperformed concat with resnet50 (0.713 vs 0.688), but the F1 actually decreased when moving from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (0.695→0.685), suggesting a possible interaction between the stronger image encoder and the fusion mechanism. Config_038 is the single closest untested variant, changing only the fusion from weighted to concat while holding all other dimensions at their best-known settings. As the final experiment, this is the most targeted exploitation test: if concat happens to interact favorably with the ViT features (e.g., preserving more complementary signal without the reweighting that may have diluted class-specific image cues), it could yield a new best. If not, it confirms the weighted-fusion advantage is robust across image encoders, solidifying confidence in config_039 as the final answer. No other untested configuration offers a more direct, single-variable comparison to the current best."
